{
  "about": "Terminal Claude draws a reply as it writes it and hands each batch of finished lines to the MessageDisplay hook. The first batch opens the reply as a message still being written, later ones extend it, and the transcript row the reply becomes takes it over, whole. Claude writes rows in the order it draws replies, so a row whose reply was not drawn yet lands under its own key and that reply's late batch draws nothing. A reply cut short ends as it was drawn. A batch that arrives after the turn ended draws nothing.",
